        {
          "passage_id": "22185730:abstract:402:526:44f7e0e67f7e",
          "paper_id": "22185730",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "In the present study, we showed that PP2A dephosphorylated tau at several phosphorylation sites with different efficiencies.",
          "score": 0.6396483182907104,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "22185730:abstract:997:1244:da0c9fa5ddfe",
          "paper_id": "22185730",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "The overall alterations in tau phosphorylation induced by PP2A inhibition were the result of the combined effects of both reduced tau dephosphorylation due to PP2A inhibition directly and reduced phosphorylation by GSK-3beta due to its inhibition.",
          "score": 0.6016862392425537,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "22185730:abstract:291:401:54b8cf10ef76",
          "paper_id": "22185730",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "However, the effects of PP2A down-regulation on site-specific tau hyperphosphorylation is not well understood.",
          "score": 0.5886133909225464,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "3113630:abstract:921:1040:396148831a8a",
          "paper_id": "3113630",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "The activity of the HDAC4 phosphatase, protein phosphatase 2A (PP2A), is downregulated by ATM-mediated phosphorylation.",
          "score": 0.8345490097999573,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "3113630:abstract:1041:1154:9f000551dea0",
          "paper_id": "3113630",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "In ATM deficiency, enhanced PP2A activity leads to HDAC4 dephosphorylation and the nuclear accumulation of HDAC4.",
          "score": 0.828702449798584,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "3113630:abstract:868:920:0d149cd2e280",
          "paper_id": "3113630",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "To remain cytoplasmic, HDAC4 must be phosphorylated.",
